T-Bone wrote:
> So I got to wondering - what is the reason that some levels aren't
> eligible for bones?  Is it a technical issue?  Game balance?
> Something else?

Any level on which bones can be generated is a level in which there
cannot be generated something essential to winning the game, in case a
player picked up the item, leaves, drops it, comes back and dies.  So,
the last level of Vlad's Tower, the Quest Goal, the top of the Wizards
Tower and the Sanctum are completely out of the question.

If the Quest Start level is eligable for bones, the player could
potentially get around an angry leader by loading a bones level in
which the staircase is already present, or be trapped out of the Quest
by a leader made angry through no fault of his own.

The wand of wishing in the Castle is an important reward, and it would
suck if a player emptied it of charges then inconsiderately died.
Also, a major game puzzle is the code to the castle drawbridge, it
would be kinda silly for your god to give you the code to the door if
it's already smashed to bits when you get there.

The challenge of some levels is dependent on the existence of certain
pre-generated monsters.  Mine End and Medusa are like this, I suspect
the two other levels of the Wizard's Tower as well, and also the
Elemental Planes and, especially, Astral.

